{"nodes": [{"id": "recovered_fault_f67_4_alpha_sample_is_filtered_f67_4", "label": "Fault F67.4 \u2014 the \u0394\u03b4 measurement basis is a 10% sample filtered by the `fail` set", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "recovered/FAULT-F67.4-ALPHA-SAMPLE-IS-FILTERED.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_fault_f67_4_alpha_sample_is_filtered_alpha_sample_42_of_419", "label": "\u03b1 rests on 42 of 419 triples", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/FAULT-F67.4-ALPHA-SAMPLE-IS-FILTERED.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "377 \u03b1 triples are blocked by a channel in `fail` (351 of them by a failed d channel) across 94 distinct Z, and the triple is skipped silently with no warning and no count. The missing 90% is not ordinary missing data: it is a null produced by the solver at places where the field has a value the instrument did not return."}, {"id": "recovered_fault_f67_4_alpha_sample_is_filtered_l_dependent_survival", "label": "Survival falls and median \u03b1 rises monotonically with l", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/FAULT-F67.4-ALPHA-SAMPLE-IS-FILTERED.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "s\u2192p 50.0% survival at median \u03b1 0.5276, p\u2192d 11.3% at 1.0688, d\u2192f 7.1% at 1.5017 \u2014 a factor of seven in survival between the transition with the lowest \u03b1 and the one with the highest, along the very axis \u00a75 reads as its result. The confound runs both ways: diffuseness plausibly drives both the convergence failure and the defect decrement, in which case \u00a75 stands. Nothing here distinguishes them, and proposing a mechanism in the session that raised the doubt is barred by F65.1."}], "edges": [{"source": "recovered_fault_f67_4_alpha_sample_is_filtered_f6